  "contentCreated": "2020-05-01T00:00:00Z",
  "origin": "24 Common Crawl shards (2020-05 to 2023-06, about a quarter of all available shards — the rest were not used to fit the OLMo project's compute budget). Processed with the cc_net pipeline: linearized HTML to plain text, deduplicated by URL (53% of duplicates removed), language identification (FastText, English threshold 0.5; ~45% of Common Crawl is English), quality filters (C4 line-ending rules + Gopher rules), content filters (toxicity via Jigsaw-trained FastText classifier, PII masking), and Bloom-filter paragraph deduplication (19.01% removed). ~2,415B tokens, 4,600M documents. The license field points at the Common Crawl terms of use; the underlying web pages are under heterogeneous licenses (the per-document multi-license aggregate problem, Gap B). This record shares the structural pattern with the BLOOM/ROOTS OSCAR record and the Pleias Common Corpus web components: a web-crawl-derived dataset whose single representative license IRI cannot faithfully represent the per-document license mix. See notes/stress-test-olmo-dolma.md. Dolma was initially released under the AI2 ImpACT license (medium-risk artifact) and later switched to ODC-BY; the ODC-BY license applies retroactively to copies downloaded under the ImpACT license (per AI2's license-change blog post), but the 0.0.1 schema cannot express that a dataset's license changed over time — see notes/stress-test-olmo-dolma.md (Gap H).",
  "custodyChain": [
    {
      "agent": "https://commoncrawl.org/",
      "action": "published-24-open-web-crawl-shards-2020-05-to-2023-06",
      "startTime": "2020-05-01T00:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "agent": "https://huggingface.co/allenai",
      "action": "processed-with-ccnet-pipeline-and-filtered-for-english-quality-toxicity-pii",
